      "side": 1,
      "message": "The step was renamed to \"VitePress\" and its cd docs/.vitepress/dist was updated in this same file, but node-version: \u002712.x\u0027 is left in place [Pre-existing]. npm run docs:build now runs vitepress build docs. VitePress 1.6.4 depends on Vite (^5.4.14; this repo pins vite 6.4.1) and declares engines.node ^18 || \u003e\u003d20; it cannot execute on Node 12. Additionally npm ci under Node 12 ships npm 6, which does not support the regenerated lockfileVersion: 3 lockfile.\n\nWhy: On merge to master this workflow publishes https://openbmc.github.io/webui-vue/ (per the commit message). With Node 12 the npm ci/npm run docs:build steps fail, so the documentation site silently stops updating — defeating the purpose of the change. Jenkins does not catch this because it runs on a modern Node, so the regression only surfaces post-merge. The commit message\u0027s \"leaves the existing Node setting alone\" is a conscious choice, but it is incompatible with the new toolchain.\n\nRecommendation: Bump the deploy workflow to a supported Node (and ideally modernize the pinned actions while touching the file)\n\n```\n- name: Generate static VitePress files\n  uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n  with:\n      node-version: \u002720.x\u0027\n- run: npm ci\n- run: npm run docs:build\n```",
